==English==

{{Webster}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} ''[[exclamare]], [[exclamatum]]''; [[ex]] + [[clamare]] to ''cry out''; confer {{etyl|fro}} ''[[exclamer]]''. See [[clam]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|eɪm}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To cry out from earnestness or passion; to utter with vehemence; to call out or declare loudly; to protest vehemently; to vociferate; to shout; as, to exclaim against oppression with wonder or astonishment.

